  "lessons": [
    "The pale rubbery edge at the bottom of a shoulder hung by the shank is the blade cartilage, not a brisket flap.",
    "Find the blade ridge by feel first and mark it; every shoulder cut is located from it.",
    "Only one tenderloin came out. Get both before or right after quartering.",
    "On the inside face, the pale whitish patch with rough red tissue at the bottom is also blade cartilage. The brisket is the thick flap that pulls away from the shoulder along a seam."
